{"id":"48db2fcda23ce31d","group":"58","path":"58/batch14/58-thm-suslin-hypothesis.md","title":"Suslin Hypothesis","display":"thm-suslin-hypothesis — Suslin Hypothesis","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-suslin-hypothesis","aliases":["58-thm-suslin-hypothesis","Suslin Hypothesis"],"display":"thm-suslin-hypothesis — Suslin Hypothesis","depends_on":["[[../batch07/58-df-suslin-tree.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-suslin-hypothesis"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-suslin-hypothesis</span><span>Suslin Hypothesis</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-suslin-hypothesis — Suslin Hypothesis"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"47ecd1e17d0a4400\" href=\"?note=47ecd1e17d0a4400\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-suslin-tree.md\">../batch07/58-df-suslin-tree.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T,R\\in V\">\\(T,R\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SuslinTree}\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{SuslinTree}\\subseteq V^2\\)</span>（see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"47ecd1e17d0a4400\" href=\"?note=47ecd1e17d0a4400\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-suslin-tree.md\">../batch07/58-df-suslin-tree.md</a>）</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SH}\\in\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{SH}\\in\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}suslin\\text{-}hypothesis} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{SH}\\leftrightarrow\\neg\\exists T,R\\in V\\;\\mathrm{SuslinTree}(T,R)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}suslin\\text{-}hypothesis} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{SH}\\leftrightarrow\\neg\\exists T,R\\in V\\;\\mathrm{SuslinTree}(T,R)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>本式采用上游的二元 Suslin 树谓词，因而量化树的载集与树序；不把它降元为未定义的一元谓词。</li>\n<li>Suslin (1920) posed the corresponding problem about linear orders.</li>\n<li>Jensen (1968): <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Diamond \\Rightarrow\">\\(\\Diamond \\Rightarrow\\)</span> Suslin tree exists.</li>\n<li>Relative to the consistency of ZFC, both SH and its negation are consistent with ZFC.</li>\n<li>SH does not by itself assert that every Aronszajn tree is special.</li>\n<li>Jech–Tennenbaum forcing gives a model of SH from suitable consistency assumptions.</li>\n<li>SH relates to: topology, order theory, combinatorics.</li>\n<li>An Aronszajn tree is an <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega_1\">\\(\\omega_1\\)</span>-tree with no uncountable branch.</li>\n<li>Special Aronszajn tree = union of countably many antichains.</li>\n<li>Martin's Axiom together with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\neg\\mathrm{CH}\">\\(\\neg\\mathrm{CH}\\)</span> implies SH.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch07/58-df-suslin-tree.md","status":"resolved","id":"47ecd1e17d0a4400","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-suslin-tree.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch07/58-df-suslin-tree.md","status":"resolved","id":"47ecd1e17d0a4400","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{SuslinTree}\\subseteq V^2$（see [[../batch07/58-df-suslin-tree.md]]）","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"T,R\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SuslinTree}\\subseteq V^2","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SH}\\in\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}suslin\\text{-}hypothesis} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{SH}\\leftrightarrow\\neg\\exists T,R\\in V\\;\\mathrm{SuslinTree}(T,R)","display":true},{"tex":"\\Diamond \\Rightarrow","display":false},{"tex":"\\omega_1","display":false},{"tex":"\\neg\\mathrm{CH}","display":false}],"bytes":1395,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4452","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch14/58-thm-suslin-hypothesis.md|58-thm-suslin-hypothesis]]（batch14）"},{"id":"7334957c6d59eacc","anchor":"ref-271","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[58-thm-0-sharp.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-condensation.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-definability.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-generic-extension.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-is-transitive.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-satisfies-GCH.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-satisfies-ZFC.md]]\n[[58-thm-MM.md]]\n[[58-thm-V-equal-L.md]]\n[[58-thm-V-equals-L.md]]\n[[58-thm-absoluteness-calculation.md]]\n[[58-thm-ac-wellorder-equivalent.md]]\n[[58-thm-aleph-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-analytic-completeness.md]]\n[[58-thm-analytic-set-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-baire-category-theory.md]]\n[[58-thm-baire-category.md]]\n[[58-thm-banach-tarski.md]]\n[[58-thm-beth-function-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-boolean-valued-model.md]]\n[[58-thm-borel-cardinality.md]]\n[[58-thm-borel-determinacy-proof.md]]\n[[58-thm-bounded-forcing-axioms.md]]\n[[58-thm-cantor.md]]\n[[58-thm-cardinal-multiplication.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-filter-properties.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-guessing.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-intersection-proper.md]]\n[[58-thm-club-intersection.md]]\n[[58-thm-coanalytic-separation.md]]\n[[58-thm-coding-universe.md]]\n[[58-thm-cofinality-regular.md]]\n[[58-thm-cohen-forcing-CH.md]]\n[[58-thm-collapse-forcing.md]]\n[[58-thm-compactness.md]]\n[[58-thm-consistency-strength-hierarchy.md]]\n[[58-thm-continuum-hypothesis.md]]\n[[58-thm-countable-choice.md]]\n[[58-thm-covering-lemma.md]]\n[[58-thm-dense-set-lemma.md]]\n[[58-thm-dependen